\begin_layout Standard
Question 1.8 :
 Two swimmers leave point A on one bank of the river to reach point B lying right across on the other bank.
 One of them crosses the river along the straight line AB while the other swims at right angles to the stream and then walks the distance that he has been carried away by the stream to get to point B.
 What was the velocity u of his walking if both swimmers reached the destination simultaneously?
 The stream velocity 
\begin_inset Formula $v_{o}$
\end_inset

 = 2.0 km/hour and the velocity v' of each swimmer with respect to water equals 2.5 km per hour.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Solution Case I :
 Swimmer swims with final velocity along AB,
 this case is also called the Shortest Path case.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
