\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We see that 
\begin_inset Formula $\overrightarrow{v'}+\overrightarrow{v_{o}}=\overrightarrow{v}$
\end_inset

 and they form a right triangle
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\Rightarrow v=\sqrt{v'^{2}-v_{o}^{2}}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
time to reach point B = 
\begin_inset Formula $\dfrac{AB}{\sqrt{v'^{2}-v_{o}^{2}}}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Case II :
 Swimmer swims at right angle to the stream,
 this would require the Shortest Time in crossing the river but the problem requires that he would have to walk to get to B.
\end_layout

